# =============================================================================
# Prepyo Frontend Configuration (Vite + React)
# =============================================================================
# This app is a static single-page build. It has no server of its own: every
# request it makes goes to the Go API backend, hosted separately at
# https://github.com/SaurabhThakulla/Prepyo-Backend.
#
# In production the Go binary serves this build alongside /api/v1, so the two
# share an origin and the session cookie works with no configuration at all.
# Nothing here is read in a production build.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev is the one case where the app and the API are on different ports, so Vite
# proxies /api/v1/* to the backend to recreate that single origin (see
# vite.config.ts). Without it the browser treats the session cookie as
# third-party and drops it.
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8080

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google sign-in
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The OAuth 2.0 Web application client ID from Google Cloud Console
# (APIs & Services > Credentials). It is public by design — the browser sends it
# to Google to render the sign-in button — so it is VITE_-prefixed and ends up in
# the bundle. The backend must be given the same id as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID: it
# verifies every ID token against it, and a mismatch rejects every sign-in.
#
# Authorised JavaScript origins for the client must list every origin the app is
# served from, http://localhost:3000 included.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sample data (frontend-only development)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Issue reporting has moved
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The "Report an issue" dialog used to post to a Next route in this repo, and
# GMAIL_USER / GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD / REPORT_EMAIL_TO lived here. That endpoint is
# POST /api/v1/report on the Go backend now, so those three belong in the
# backend's environment instead. Nothing in this repo reads them.
